      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Based on standard DC-4 architecture, the biggest power hogs are typically idle-but-active background services like telemetry agents, log shippers, and ML inference caches that poll continuously. These often aren't needed for the 5ms critical path—you can batch their data or run them on a separate low-power node. Also, look at any redundant replication modules (e.g., live cross-cluster sync) that might be over-provisioned; if you have a nearline backup, you can drop the real-time mirror. Finally, spin down any pre-warmed containers or JIT compilers that aren't serving traffic during off-peak; they burn CPU for zero latency benefit. For a true 15% cut, I'd suspend the non-critical analytics dashboard aggregator and move its cron jobs to a 5-minute interval.",
